  "question": {
    "text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> wide truck is moving with a uniform speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> along a straight horizontal road. A pedestrian starts to cross the road with a uniform speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&nbsp;moving in a straight line,&nbsp;</mo></math>when the truck is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> away from him. The minimum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo></math>&nbsp;so that he can cross the road safely is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0030_38bcb1918651.jpg\" style=\"width: 256px; height: 136px;\" />"
